course: dictionary
lesson: 14561
title: A formal word for doctor
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A physician is a doctor, a person who helps people when they are ill. It is a formal word, so you will read it more than you will say it, and people use it most in the United States. «My sister felt dizzy, so Mum took her to see the physician.» The words ill and dizzy are clues: a physician is the doctor you visit when you are not well.
explain: Look at how a physician helps. «The physician listened to my chest and gave me medicine for my cough.» The medicine is the clue. A physician usually treats illness with medicine, not with surgery. Surgery means cutting open the body to fix a problem, and that is a surgeon's work.
explain: In the UK, most people say doctor or GP for this job. You may still meet the word in history books: «The royal physician looked after the king when he was sick.» A royal physician was a doctor who cared for kings and queens.
fact: A physician is a medical doctor.
fact: «Physician» is a formal word, and it is used especially in the United States.
fact: A physician usually treats illness with medicine rather than surgery.
fact: In everyday British speech, people often say doctor or GP for the same kind of job.
fact: Phrases you may read: «family physician» means the doctor a family usually visits, and «consult your physician» means ask your doctor for advice.
exercise: «The physician listened to my chest and said I had a cold.» What is a physician? | A builder who fixes old walls | A cook who works in a hospital kitchen | *A doctor who treats illness with medicine | A teacher who marks spelling tests
exercise: «The physician smiled and wrote a note for the school.» Find and copy the word that means doctor. | *physician | smiled | school | note
exercise: «Hanna's physician said she must rest in bed for a week.» What did the physician do? | *Told Hanna what she must do to get better | Took Hanna to the cinema | Cut Hanna's hair | Delivered the post to Hanna's house
test: «The royal physician looked after the king when he had a fever.» Who was a royal physician? | *A doctor who cared for a king or queen | A soldier who guarded the castle gate | A cook who made the royal feasts | A man who built the palace walls
test: Which word is the formal word for doctor, used most in the United States? | surgeon | nurse | *physician | teacher
exam: A surgeon and a physician are both doctors, but which one treats illness mainly with medicine instead of cutting? | Nurse | *Physician | Surgeon | Builder
